// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.database.entityimport androidx.room.Entityimport androidx.room.PrimaryKey/** * NOUS — Undo Action Entity (Module 10 v2 — PersistentUndoStack). * * Stores reversible system operations so the user can say "NOUS, undo that" * even after an app restart. Each row is one executed operation with its * captured pre-state (per strategy v2 Review 2 Fix A — pre-state, NOT inverse). * * ## Lifecycle * *  1. [com.roshan.persona.system.executor.SystemOperationExecutorImpl] executes *     an operation successfully + handler is reversible. *  2. Pre-state is captured via `handler.capturePreState()`. *  3. [com.roshan.persona.system.undo.PersistentUndoStack.push] inserts a row. *  4. [com.roshan.persona.system.undo.PersistentUndoStack.trim] removes rows *     beyond the last 50 (LIFO + bounded). *  5. User says "undo" → [PersistentUndoStack.pop] returns the latest row. *  6. Executor calls `handler.restorePreState(operation, preState)`. *  7. [PersistentUndoStack.confirmPop] deletes the row after successful restore. * * ## Why serialized, not typed columns? * * SystemOperation is a sealed interface with ~20 variants, each with different * parameters (Boolean on/off, Int level, String packageName, nested enums). * Storing each variant's fields as separate columns would require ~30 columns * most of which are NULL per row. A single `operation_json` column is simpler, * more maintainable, and survives schema changes when new operations are added. * * @see <a href="docs/strategy/module-10-system-strategy-v2.md">§Persistent Undo Stack</a> */@Entity(tableName = "undo_actions")data class UndoActionEntity(    /** Auto-generated row ID. Higher ID = more recent action (LIFO ordering). */    @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,    /** The operation type name (e.g., "SetTorch", "SetVolume").     *  Used for filtering + diagnostics without parsing JSON. */    val operationType: String,    /** Serialized operation (e.g., `{"on":true,"brightness":1.0}`).     *  Parsed back via [com.roshan.persona.system.undo.SystemOperationSerializer]. */    val operationJson: String,    /** Serialized pre-state captured before execution     *  (e.g., `{"previousVolume":50}`). Null if stateless. */    val preStateJson: String?,    /** Handler ID that executed this operation (e.g., "torch", "volume").     *  Used to find the right handler for restore. */    val handlerId: String,    /** Wall-clock time the operation was executed (ms since epoch). */    val timestampMs: Long,    /** Human-readable description for the undo UI     *  (e.g., "Torch turned on", "Volume set to 80"). */    val description: String,)